{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"reasoning","text":"**Planning TabBar and preview actions**\n\nTabBar supports `.flex_1()`, so I’ll use it to arrange the preview header with a flexed TabBar and action buttons. I’ll add a Settings button for preview actions but skip Refresh since it’s already present elsewhere. I’m considering simplifying settings UI by removing toggles and Back button, possibly renaming or removing the close button since no clear method exists—leaning toward just a header label without Back since settings won’t render in main now."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"reasoning","text":"**Refactoring settings to separate window with sync**\n\nI'm removing the show_settings toggle and Back button, replacing main and preview Settings actions to open a dedicated settings window via a new `open_or_create_settings_window` function. This involves creating a new settings window with its own view mode and updating routing and menu actions accordingly. To keep settings changes in sync across multiple windows (main, preview, settings), I'll implement a broadcast mechanism that updates other windows’ state when settings or config change, ensuring consistent app state without nested updates."}}
